ut that and I  that's all we would talk about we never  read in the papers like you do now how  much money this film made on Thursday or  for the weekend which my great friend  the editor of the LA Times is here  tonight davon Maharaja and davon I wish  you could be the editor of The Times in  those days when they just wrote about  cinema in that box office and now all  they care about is box office that's  that's okay  because that's what drives the business  but it didn't then and well I think I  don't know what side of that argument I  was on but I think Gaddar is the one who  survived because almost everything you  see even on television owes something to  go die jump cuts quick cuts like you do  in Mission Impossible you know guilty  yeah every seven seconds the shot  changes and in in the days when I was  making films like this it we tried to  hold the shot as long as possible we  didn't want to cut we only cut to go to  the next scene or if some guy was  standing way over there  we had a there's no way to get him in  the same frame
 

